<!-- The S.D. Cal. motion-brief's Word styles (memorandum of points and authorities); fb render builds
     docx/reference.docx from pandoc's default reference with them (tools/fb/src/docxref.rs). Pleading paper per S.D.
     Cal. Civil L.R. 5.1, as the typst template casd-motion-brief.typ: Times New Roman 14 point everywhere (the typst
     face), 24 pt exact double spacing on every body line, no space between paragraphs, first-line indent 0.5 in, US
     Letter, 1.5 in left margin, 1 in right, top and bottom margins (27 lines of 24 pt, as typst lines-per-page; CivLR 5.1 allows
     28), Word line numbering (w:lnNumType, restarting each page), and a double rule at the text's left edge
     and a single rule at its right. Headings: level 1 centered bold; level 2 (I.) and level 3 (A.) bold with
     hanging indents, level 3 italic too. docx/casd.lua writes the sections and their footers. -->
